1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:01,637
Dolphins sleep with one eye open.

2
00:00:01,657 --> 00:00:02,585
One half of the brain

3
00:00:02,585 --> 00:00:04,167
drops into deep sleep,

4
00:00:04,187 --> 00:00:05,820
while the other half stays awake.

5
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:07,177
Later, they swap.

6
00:00:07,197 --> 00:00:08,088
Scientists call it

7
00:00:08,088 --> 00:00:09,357
unihemispheric sleep.

8
00:00:09,377 --> 00:00:10,929
The leading idea is breathing.

9
00:00:10,949 --> 00:00:12,027
Dolphins are voluntary

10
00:00:12,027 --> 00:00:13,593
breathers, so half the brain

11
00:00:13,593 --> 00:00:14,725
stays awake to keep coming

12
00:00:14,725 --> 00:00:15,409
up for air.

13
00:00:15,429 --> 00:00:15,950
That's why,

14
00:00:15,950 --> 00:00:16,851
every single night,
